        "Proposed text": "A descriptive definite that names a kind of thing but not which one (\"the Bitcoin ETF\", \"the major-bank stablecoin consortium\", \"the open-access version\", \"the infrastructure\", \"the new model\") makes the claim Context-dependent: the reader must already know which ETF, consortium, version or product is meant. A capitalised, name-like phrase for a body that readers do not know is still such a kind. A group that every reader knows by its standing role (such as a press pool) counts as identified. Applies to countable things, not to abstract or mass nouns (\"the regulatory clearance\", \"the market\")."
